SUMMARY:Whackadoo Gone Wild
LOCATION:Just the Tonic at The Caves\, 253 Cowgate\, Edinburgh
DESCRIPTION:Uh oh\, The Whackadoo Boys are at it again! This time in an abs
 urdist romp to the unexplored wilds of the Channel Islands. Whackadoo Gone 
 Wild is an absurdist comedy play exploring themes of friendship\, self wort
 h and animal conservation. The heartfelt story features puppetry\, dance an
 d plenty of audience interaction. Whackadoo is a sketch duo comprised of Ca
 mbridge Footlights Isaac Kean (Chortle Student Comedy Award finalist) and A
 dam Al-janabi (as seen on BBC's SAS Rogue Heroes).\nMore info: https://come
 dyatlas.app/comedy-atlas/event/whackadoo-gone-wild/
